# Memory findings that are nginx's own, not this module's.  The valgrind job
# drives the module through ci/auth_digest.sh, which runs one foreground
# nginx (master_process off) end to end with curl and shuts it down with
# QUIT, so the pools are freed and whatever is left here belongs to nginx
# core.
#
# This is measured, not assumed: with an empty file the driver reports
# exactly this one definite loss and nothing else, and no frame from
# ngx_http_auth_digest_module.c appears in it.  nginx allocates the
# environment array once and lets the process exit reclaim it.  If a later
# nginx brings a new finding, valgrind prints a full trace; add it then, with
# a name and a reason, rather than keeping one here on the chance that it is
# still needed.

{
   nginx keeps the environment array until the process ends
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:ngx_alloc
   fun:ngx_set_environment
   ...
}
